<BaseLayout title="Demo terms | LiveDiscover"><section class="container page-section simple-page"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Know before you go</p><h1>A few<br/><i>house notes.</i></h1><p>Terms for exploring the LiveDiscover demonstration.</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>A fictional live music guide</h2><p>LiveDiscover is a concept website. All artists, tours, and event listings shown here are original fictional sample content. The Foundry Hall is fictional. Real venue names and approximate locations are used only to illustrate a regional music guide.</p><h2>No tickets or reservations</h2><p>No tickets are sold, payments taken, or real places reserved through this website. Demo RSVP entries and event drafts are stored in your browser. They do not create an agreement with a performer, venue, promoter, or ticket seller.</p><h2>Information and travel</h2><p>Do not use sample dates, venue capacities, descriptions, or directions as confirmation of a real event. Consult the venue’s official information before buying tickets or travelling.</p><h2>Your submitted material</h2><p>Only enter material you have permission to use. Demo drafts are not reviewed, published, or sent to third parties. Uploaded artwork is not stored; only its filename is retained in the local draft.</p><h2>Using the demo</h2><p>You are welcome to explore the site, save sample events, and try the forms. Do not use it to submit private information, impersonate anyone, or interfere with the service.</p><h2>Before going live</h2><p>The site operator must replace these demo notes with terms appropriate to its business, editorial process, ticketing relationships, and audience before launching a real service.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
